The DECPc XL 466 is the original in a product line that included the Celebris XL
and the Alpha XL.   DEC never divulged why the system needed so many power
connectors.  The power hookup was definitely designed by Rube Goldberg or some
other electronically deranged person.

I have never seen on-line manuals for the DECPc XL 466, but I do have the
Celebris XL service manual, which will give you some clues because of the
similarity between the two.

If you are interested in upgrading to a Pentium class processor, send me the DEC
54-series (or 50-series) part number inscribed on the main logic board, and I'll
be able to tell you what the possibilities might be.  I also kept a few power
supplies and other misc parts for these computers after parting them out and
tearing them down.

I once sold a large number of main logic board and processor upgrades for these
systems, bought surplus when DEC shuttered its Toronto-area system facility.
Now these are largely hobbyist computers, even though built like a small tank.

I also have a complete and working Alpha XL system here, if anyone is
interested.  I need to either sell it for a few bucks (not much more) or scrap
it... Ben Myers  ben_myers@charter.net

