>firmware upgrade.

Go ahead.

>Is there any reason not to do this?  Is there any reason to upgrade the 
>firmware before installing VMS?

Iff the firmware version is below MINIMUM firmware version for VMS, you
can't install VMS (only an older version of it). Iff the firmware version
is below RECOMMENDED firmware version, you can do what you planned to do...

btw: Alpha firmware is not on the VMS freeware CD (or why was it mentioned ?)
Newest Alpha Firmware can be downloaded as an CD image which you burn
(eg. on a PC) and do the firmware upgrade even before the VMS installation.
Unfortunately, the 1200 is too old for the latest firmware CD...

	ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/archive/as1200.html

