You'll want to set the jumpers to be compatible but it ought to work.
The Tandon 848 has some funky jumpering for motor control and two-sided
operation and head select using drive select, depending on where it was
last installed it may be appropriate or inappropriately set up.

Also, of course, the TM848 uses DC power to spin the disk instead of AC
like the SA801-type.  But typical power supplies used for 8" drives
shouldn't have a problem (those steppers on a SA801 got quite warm, so
there's plenty of +24V current available!)  Of course with DC powered
spindle you won't have to worry about 50Hz vs 60Hz pulleys!

Tim.



